Comprehensive Admin Expansion & UI/UX Modernization Plan
Overview & Goal
The Mound Hounds Pick'em Admin section currently manages an entire fantasy racing season, but suffers from two main issues:

Scattered, Disjointed UI/UX: Operational and maintenance features are fragmented across multiple tabs and buried inside deep disclosure accordions. For example, Season Management is hidden in an accordion inside the "Races" tab, Hall of Fame archival is an accordion in "Results", Preseason driver seeding is in "Drivers", and "Race Week" is mixed with raw database health, cron heartbeats, and error inboxes under a tab called health.
Repo/SQL Reliance for Routine Operations: Routine league administration tasks still require direct repository scripts or Supabase SQL Editor queries. Key examples include: promoting/demoting co-admins, importing historical spreadsheet leaderboards (e.g. 2026/2025 Google Sheets) into the Hall of Fame, running orphaned image cleanup in Supabase Storage, and triggering background jobs or retrieving participant emails.
This plan details the full blueprint for a subsequent coding agent to modernize the admin UI/UX into an intuitive, progressive workspace and empower the league administrator to manage the league end-to-end directly in the application.

Proposed Information Architecture & Workspace Reorganization
We will restructure the Admin workspace from 7 fragmented tabs into 8 clearly defined, single-responsibility operational hubs:

Mermaid diagram
Workspace Directory
Tab Key	Label	Scope & Primary Workflows
race-week (default)	Race Week	The weekly operational cockpit. Guides the admin through the 4 phases of race week: field freeze, pick monitoring & reminders, results import & scoring audit, and winner finalization.
seasons	Seasons & League	Dedicated league lifecycle hub. Create seasons, manage/rotate invite codes, copy signup links, upload rules documents, run pre-flight activation checks, finalize seasons, and import historical spreadsheet archives.
participants	Participants	Directory of all accounts. View participant emails, promote/demote co-admins (with safety guards), toggle season registration, manage account eligibility, and perform bulk updates.
drivers	Drivers & Groups	Opening championship seed importer, active roster toggle, driver photo gallery with "missing headshot" filter, and in-app Supabase Storage orphan image audit & cleanup.
races	Race Calendar	Focused race schedule. Create rounds, link doubleheaders (pick_window_key), correct qualifying deadlines, and upload race banners without distracting season or winner controls.
health	System Health	Dedicated DevOps center. Schema contract check, cron job status & execution logs, on-demand trigger buttons, application error inbox with resolution, searchable audit log, and test data cleanup.
recovery	Recovery	Preserves existing robust safety snapshots, backup downloads, and restore diff previews.
feedback	Feedback	Preserves existing participant issue/suggestion triage inbox with status filters.
NOTE

For backwards compatibility, existing URL parameters (tab=results, tab=health, tab=races, etc.) will continue to work seamlessly. tab=results will redirect to the results phase of tab=race-week or render as a focused results view.

Detailed New Administrative Capabilities (Eliminating Repo/SQL Reliance)
1. Admin Role Delegation & Co-Admin Management
Current state: Admin roles must be manually assigned via raw SQL in Supabase SQL Editor (UPDATE profiles SET role = 'admin' WHERE id = '...').
New In-App Feature:
In Participants, each row displays the participant's current role with a button: "Promote to Admin" or "Demote to Participant".
Clicking opens a confirmation dialog detailing the permissions granted or revoked.
Defensive Invariants:
Self-demotion prevention: An admin cannot demote themselves.
Last-admin guard: Demotion is refused if the user is the only active admin.
Audit logging: Calls recordAdminAudit recording who changed the role, target profile ID, and before/after states.
Cache & session revalidation: Revalidates paths so the change takes effect immediately.
2. Historical Hall of Fame Spreadsheet Importer
Current state: Past seasons from spreadsheets (e.g. 2025/2026 prelaunch) require manual database inserts or custom scripts (docs/OPERATIONS_GUIDE.md:137-143).
New In-App Feature:
In Seasons, an "Import Historical Season" tool.
Inputs: Season Year (e.g. 2026), Race Count (e.g. 17), and a large paste area accepting TSV/CSV copied directly from Google Sheets or Excel.
Required columns: Rank, Team Name, Total Points (with optional breakdown).
Live Validation & Preview:
Automatically identifies the champion (Rank 1).
Detects ties and alerts if an unresolved tie for first place exists.
Flags duplicate team names or invalid point totals.
Shows a table preview of the parsed entries before saving.
Submission: Calls the existing atomic stored procedure public.finalize_hall_of_fame_season(p_season_year, p_race_count, p_entries).
3. In-App Storage Orphan Image Audit & Purge
Current state: Admins have to run npm run cleanup:orphaned-images and npm run cleanup:orphaned-images -- --apply via terminal.
New In-App Feature:
In Drivers, a "Storage Media Maintenance" panel.
"Audit Orphaned Images" button: Scans the driver-headshots and race-title-images buckets against drivers.image_url and races.title_image_url.
Displays summary: Stored files count, Referenced count, Orphaned count, and Total reclaimable space (KB/MB).
Lists the orphaned file paths in an expandable preview.
"Delete Orphaned Images" button: Secure server action using the service role client that removes only unreferenced files and logs the action to admin_audit_events.
4. Season Invite Code & Shareable Registration Links
Current state: Setting an invite code exists in an accordion, but there is no way to copy a pre-filled invite link, check if a code is currently set, or test registration readiness.
New In-App Feature:
In Seasons, each season card displays:
Invite code status ("Configured on [date]" vs "Required").
"Copy Signup Link": Copies https://moundhoundspickem.app/signup?code=... or /season-registration?code=... with the private code embedded for easy distribution via email/text.
"Rotate Code" modal with validation (8-64 characters, confirmation match).
Rules Document: Upload PDF directly to Supabase storage or set an external HTTPS URL.
5. Participant Email Visibility & Manual Enrollment Overrides
Current state: Admin only sees team_name and full_name; user emails in auth.users are hidden unless the admin opens the Supabase dashboard.
New In-App Feature:
On the server, load user emails for admins using createServiceRoleSupabaseClient().auth.admin.listUsers().
In Participants, search matches on email address in addition to name and team name.
Displays user email clearly next to team name, making it easy to identify members who report login or reminder issues.
Season Enrollment Switcher: Allows an admin to manually mark a participant as "Registered" or "Declined" for any specific season.
Bulk Actions: Select multiple participants to toggle account eligibility (is_active) or register them for the upcoming season.
6. Guided Race Week Cockpit
Current state: AdminResultsWorkspace renders 7 competing disclosures (dropdown, Indy 500 qualifying order, results import, scoring audit, manual entry, publish form, season closeout, saved rows) in a single overwhelming stack.
New In-App Feature:
Replace the disclosure pile with a 4-Phase Progressive Race Flow:
Phase 1: Preparation & Deadline: View/freeze driver field snapshot; import Indy 500 qualifying order (if Indy 500); correct qualifying deadline if rain delay occurs.
Phase 2: Picks & Reminders: Visual submission counter (X/Y submitted); list of missing participants with one-click "Copy missing emails"; reminder queue health and retry failed deliveries; send test email to admin.
Phase 3: Results & Audit: Official IndyCar results paste/file upload; live Scoring Audit preview (calculated team scores, tiebreak deltas, projected fantasy winner); single explicit "Publish Results" action requiring official winning speed.
Phase 4: Winner Finalization: Shows official fantasy winner; provides "Calculate Winner Now" button (to immediately finalize without waiting 15 minutes) or manual override.
7. On-Demand Background Job Triggers
Current state: If an hourly fantasy-winner calculation fails or needs immediate execution, the admin must wait for pg_cron or run SQL.
New In-App Feature:
In System Health, provide an on-demand button: "Run Fantasy Winner Check Now" (invokes finalizeDueRaceWinners()).
Provide "Send Test Reminder" and "Retry Failed Reminders" in the email queue card.
